To add a link to every post on your website, you'll need to make changes to your Nginx configuration and your HTML template. Here's a step-by-step guide:

**Step 1: Modify your Nginx configuration**

Add the following block to your first `server` block (the one that serves the static HTML content):
```nginx
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    server_name www.askfundu.com;
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;

    # ... (rest of the configuration)

    # Add a location block for posts
    location ~ /.+\.html$ {
        rewrite ^(.*)$ /post-link$1 permanent;
    }
}
```
This configuration will redirect all requests for HTML files (e.g., `post1.html`, `post2.html`, etc.) to new URLs with a `/post-link` prefix.

**Step 2: Modify your HTML template**

In your HTML template (e.g., `index.html`), add a link to each post. You can do this using a HTML anchor tag (`<a>`) and the `post-link` prefix:
```html
<!-- Assuming you have a list of posts with links somewhere in your HTML -->
<ul>
    {% for post in posts %}
        <li>
            <a href="/post-link{{ post.url }}">{{ post.title }}</a>
        </li>
    {% endfor %}
</ul>
```
Replace `posts` with the actual variable name and `post.url` and `post.title` with the properties of your post object.

**Step 3: Update your post creation script**

When creating a new post, update the script that generates the HTML file to include the `post-link` prefix. For example, if you're using a template engine like Jinja2, you can modify the template file like this:
```jinja
